# 6. Greeting formatter (bench/references.md §6). A function that builds a
# piece of text: two string literals joined around a variable, chosen by a
# conditional.
#
#   λx0:Str. λx1:Bool. if x1 then "Good evening, " ++ x0 ++ "." else "hi " ++ x0 ++ "!"
#
# The only change from the reference is currying: `nothing` has no
# multi-argument functions, so `greet(name, formal)` is two nested lambdas.

# λx0:Str. ⦇⦈
construct-lam
move-parent
rename x0
set-ann Str
move-child 0

# λx1:Bool. ⦇⦈
construct-lam
move-parent
rename x1
set-ann Bool
move-child 0

# if x1 then ⦇⦈ else ⦇⦈
construct-if
construct-var x1
move-next-sibling

# then: "Good evening, " ++ x0 ++ "."
construct-str "Good evening, "
construct-binop concat
construct-var x0
move-parent
construct-binop concat
construct-str "."

# else: "hi " ++ x0 ++ "!"
move-parent
move-next-sibling
construct-str "hi "
construct-binop concat
construct-var x0
move-parent
construct-binop concat
construct-str "!"
